From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:34:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Science pages of the documentation, with hand-drawn
 sketches

Two pages explain how the toolbox works, with the equations of the code:
- How it works: terrain parameters (Horn gradients, horizons, sky view
  factor), TopoSUB sampling, horizontal and vertical interpolation,
  accumulation windows, solar geometry and shading, computing by blocks.
- Variables and options: temperature (surface effect: REDCAPP, DReaMIT),
  humidity, pressure, wind (10 m blend, MicroMet), precipitation (lapse
  factor, hemispheres, rain/snow partition), shortwave (empirical or ERA5
  split, Beer's law, illumination, isotropic or Hay-Davies diffuse,
  terrain reflection), longwave (clear-sky and cloud emissivity, terrain
  emission and its temperature), and a table of all options.

Seven sketches are drawn as clean SVG in doc/sketches/src and turned into
hand-drawn figures by doc/sketches/roughen.js (rough.js, Patrick Hand font
embedded as a subset, OFL). Equations render with MathJax (pymdownx
arithmatex); new references in refs.bib.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
